.SH CONFIGURATION & SCHEMA SPECIFICATIONS
.SS Settings Store (bashmenu.yml)
Stores nested, dot-notation accessible key-value settings. Any nested path (e.g.
settings.dns.ipv4) can be interpolated inside menu files or actions.
The special setting
.I settings.status_gutter
defines which system badges (such as {user}, {battery}, or {date_time_24}) are
displayed in the bottom right corner (the status gutter). This value is specified
as a string of badges separated by pipe symbols (|). The engine will fit as many
of these badges as possible based on the terminal's available width.
.SS Menu Structure (bashmenu.mnu)
The menu is defined as a hierarchical YAML options list. Options can utilize the
following configuration keys:
.TP
.B type
Option action type (see SECTION TYPES).
.TP
.B label
Row label. Can use dynamic placeholders.
.TP
.B icon
Icon tags utilizing brackets: {nf:[char]:[nerd-font hex]:[emoji]}.
.TP
.B action
Shell command, script, or editor file path.
.TP
.B template, target, block_id
Path, destination, and unique tag for dynamic templates (inject_block).
.TP
.B quiet, stream, interactive, external, user_mode
Execution privilege and console behavior flags.
.TP
.B key, picker, start_dir, masked
Dot-notation settings key and visual configuration chooser flags.
.TP
.B show_whitespace, tab_to_spaces, tabstop
Text editor layout configurations.
.TP
.B on_yes, on_no, message
Confirmation options and alert prompts.
.SH SECTION TYPES
.TP
.B submenu
Opens a nested submenu options list.
.TP
.B command
Executes a standard shell command.
.TP
.B script
Launches an external script or executable.
.TP
.B config
Prompts user to edit setting value.
.TP
.B toggle
True/False/Cancel settings toggle modal.
.TP
.B editor
Opens file in built-in Nano-style editor.
.TP
.B confirm
Launches Yes/No confirmation dialog box.
.TP
.B message
Informational alert or popup dialog.
.TP
.B python
Dispatches internal Python routine.
.TP
.B inject_block
Installs or uninstalls template blocks inside profiles.
.TP
.B theme_selector
Launches list of registered color themes.
.TP
.B divider
Renders an aesthetic non-selectable horizontal line separator. Supports optional length and char attributes.
.TP
.B back
Navigates back to the preceding submenu level.
.TP
.B exit
Shuts down the menu interface completely.
.SH DYNAMIC DIRECTIVES & SYSTEM PLACEHOLDERS
.SS Dynamic Input Directives
These directives prompt the user inside curses dialogs, replacing the placeholder
with the chosen value prior to action execution.
.TP
.B {param}
Prompts for a single-line text value using a modal input box.
.TP
.B {file_picker}
Launches a visual file chooser dialog box.
.TP
.B {dir_picker}
Launches a visual directory chooser dialog box.
.SS Picker Auto-Starting Folders
Preceding file/directory pickers with a folder path (e.g.
"{templates_dir}/{file_picker}" or "~/projects/{dir_picker}") causes the engine
to automatically launch the visual chooser inside that directory.
.SS System Placeholders
The following placeholders are auto-interpolated inside actions or templates:
.TP
.B {user}, {username}
Current system username.
.TP
.B {host}
System host name.
.TP
.B {user-mode}
Current privilege mode ("root" if running with root/sudo privileges, otherwise "user").
.TP
.B {version}
Script version (e.g., 0.0.1).
.TP
.B {home}
User's absolute home directory path.
.TP
.B {bashmenu_dir}
Application script directory.
.TP
.B {templates_dir}, {scripts_dir}
Templates and scripts folders paths.
.TP
.B {bashrc}, {vimrc}, {bash_aliases}
Path files system profiles.
.TP
.B {date_time_12}, {date_time_24}
12-hour and 24-hour formatted date-time.
.TP
.B {date}
Current date (YYYY-MM-DD).
.TP
.B {time_12}, {time_24}
12-hour and 24-hour current time.
.TP
.B {battery}
Current battery percentage (e.g. 84% or N/A). Includes a 5-second performance cache.
.TP
.B {utc_seconds}
Current UTC epoch seconds.
.TP
.B {window_width}, {window_height}
Current active window width (columns) and height (lines) in characters.
.TP
.B {ascii:decimal}
Prints character corresponding to decimal code (uses CP437 for extended ASCII, e.g. {ascii:168} resolves to ¿).
.TP
.B {settings.dot_key}
Dot-notation configuration lookup from bashmenu.yml (e.g., {settings.status_gutter}).
.SS Nerd Fonts & Emoji Adaptive Resolution
The application resolves icons dynamically using three properties: a fallback
ASCII character, a Nerd Font PUA code point, and a Unicode emoji icon:
.RS
.B {nf:[char]:[nerd-font hex]:[emoji-glyph]}
.RE
Precedence is evaluated as follows:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Emoji Icon (Unicode capable)
\- Chosen if system is Unicode capable and emoji is provided.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Nerd Font Glyph (Nerd Fonts enabled)
\- Chosen if system is Unicode capable, use_nerd_fonts is true, and hex is
provided. Translates and renders the Nerd Font glyph.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Fallback ASCII Character
\- Displayed if Unicode is unsupported or both above fields are missing.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Wiped Default
\- Resolves to empty string if all are missing, collapsing the icon column.
.SH MODULARITY & PLUGINS
.SS Dynamic Block Injection
The inject_block type installs templates inside profile files (e.g. .bashrc).
It wraps the template in markers (# CODEBLOCK:block_id:START/END) to manage
seamless interactive installs, updates, and uninstalls.
.SS In-Process Python Plugins (external: false)
Python script items of type "script" can set "external: false" to run inside
bashmenu's parent process, avoiding terminal flashes. Plugins must implement
"def main(stdscr)".
